 This dynamic role contains Field Service activities such as preventive & corrective maintenance, retrofits and commissioning activities, making it ideal for those with hands-on attitude, and a clear customer focus.
 We’re looking for an all-rounder who can support our service organization in Canada. This will require you to collaborate with internal teams and our customers. If you’re technically solid, like to travel and have a clear customer focus, we’d love to hear from you.
 Main Tasks 
 Ensure the efficient performance of services delivered to our customers in Canada and occasionally worldwide;
 Execute preventive and corrective maintenance activities at customer facilities according to Sécheron standards;
 Implement retrofits and modernization projects in collaboration with internal teams and customers;
 Provide supervision of installation, testing, commissioning and occasionally customer trainings on Sécheron equipment;
 Execute audits of existing equipment;
 Performing repairs at the company’s facilities in Montreal;
 Elaboration of technical intervention reports and templates;
 Support to Sales Engineer on substation surveys and permissions to site access;
 Support Sales team with the elaboration of repair quotations;
 Promote proactively new service centered business opportunities during customer visits, such as spare parts sales, repairs, on-site services, retrofits, trainings, etc.;
 Provide support on DC products, including: 
 - DC switchgear, high-speed breakers, and panels; 
 - Rectifiers, power converters, and voltage limiting devices;
 - Multi-function protection relays and custom electro-mechanical solutions;
 Support on the management of stock of spare parts and tools.
 Bachelor’s degree in electrical engineering; or relevant technical experience will also be considered;
 Minimum requirement: High school diploma or GED combined with industry experience;
 Field Service background in the field of installation, testing and maintenance of electrical equipment with custom electro-mechanical solutions;
 Prior experience in power distribution, switchgear manufacturing, or similar roles (3+ years preferred);
 Familiarity with DC power systems (Low Voltage and Medium Voltage up to 3kV);
 Safety training and certification including OSHA card, current basic first aid and CPR certification;
 Systematic way of working, hand-on approach;
 Strong customer orientation, good communication skills and the ability to move within the customer organization;
 Self-motivated, team-oriented, and adaptable in complex technical environments;
 Ability to analyze technical requirements and create clear, accurate solutions;
 Domestic travel: up to 80%;
 Occasional international travel.
